# source: spec
# spec: docs/protocol/ni-framing.md#on-the-wire
# provenance: PV-0001, PV-0002, PV-0003, PV-0004, PV-0200
# kind: ni-stream
# description: A keep-alive ping as it arrives from the server: an ordinary frame with length 8 whose payload is NI_PING\0.
# derivation: u32 BE length 8 (PV-0001, PV-0002) counting only the payload (PV-0003), then the 8 literal bytes of PV-0004; PV-0200 states that a ping travels in exactly this framed form.
# expect.frames: 1
# expect.frame.1.offset: 4
# expect.frame.1.length: 8
# expect.error: none
# expect.trailing: 0
hex:
00 00 00 08                                       # length 8, u32 BE
4E 49 5F 50 49 4E 47 00                           # N I _ P I N G \0
